 ('Reading · A biography',bio('Simone de Beauvoir (1908–1986)',['Simone de Beauvoir, **born** in Paris in 1908, **studied** philosophy at the Sorbonne and **went on to teach** it in secondary schools. **Her partnership with Jean-Paul Sartre**, **which lasted** until his death, **was** intellectual as well as personal. In *The Ethics of Ambiguity* (1947) she **argued** that freedom is **achieved** only **through** the freedom of others.','Her best-known work, *The Second Sex* (1949), **examined** how women **have been defined** in relation to men. Its most-quoted line, “One is not born, but rather becomes, a woman,” **has been** debated ever since. **She also wrote** novels; *The Mandarins* **received** the Prix Goncourt in 1954. **Widely regarded** as a **founding voice** of modern feminism, she **died** in Paris in 1986.'],years='1908–1986',facts=[('Born','Paris, França'),('Obra principal','O Segundo Sexo (1949)'),('Prêmio','Prix Goncourt (1954)')],gloss=[('partnership','parceria'),('ambiguity','ambiguidade'),('founding','fundador'),('quoted','citado')])),
